    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with significant firepower, led by **Kyle Tucker** (82.82) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Both stand out as our elite anchors against favorable matchups; **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a soft 5.19 xERA assignment against Jack Kochanowicz, while **Gunnar Henderson** holds strong value despite a potentially tough matchup against Littell, bolstered by a 14% platoon edge and a robust BvP history. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) rounds out the top tier, leveraging his dynamic platoon advantage against Shane Baz to provide efficient production in the middle infield. We are keeping a close watch on the lineups for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Josh Jung**, as late-breaking changes to batting order or defensive configurations could shift these projections.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Coby Mayo** (51.44), who fell just shy of the start threshold. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same favorable matchup against Littell that elevates **Gunnar Henderson**, he is handicapped by a projected #7 spot in the order and a negative platoon split that limits his day-to-day upside compared to **Brady House** (56.25). **Brady House** gets the nod for his superior slot efficiency, despite the concern regarding a slow delivery from the opposition that might tempt aggressive base-running strategies we aren't fully banking on today. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.49) remains a locked-in start, as his high xwOBA (0.379) provides a solid floor even in a neutral-to-negative platoon situation against Hanifee. We are monitoring **Drake Baldwin** closely, as his sub-50 score (46.72) is heavily suppressed by an elite opposing arm (2.92 xERA), making him a marginal play today who remains in the lineup only due to positional scarcity.",
